  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 131 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nOn Wednesday and Wednesday night the stacked cyclone will\ncontinue to move away from our area, across Wisconsin and up to\naround Lake Superior. A large cloud/light rain shield wrapping\naround its backside will pivot across Iowa during this time,\nespecially the northern half or so of the state, and generally\nmake for gray and blustery conditions with areas of light\nrainfall. These conditions will persist from Wednesday right\nthrough Thursday, with high temperatures on both days ranging \nonly in the upper 40s north to mid/upper 50s southeast; notably \ncooler than we have seen in the last couple of weeks or so.\n\nFrom Friday onward the forecast is much more quiet and dry as we\nenter a period of west northwesterly 500 MB steering flow with\nperiods of modest ridging therein. No rain is forecast during\nthis time, and while Friday highs will remain cool in the upper\n40s/50s once again, a slow warming trend will then bring them up\ninto the upper 50s/lower 60s by next Monday. This will make for\na very pleasant, if slightly cool, late autumn weekend across\nthe region.",
